---
const plan = [
  ['Choose the catalog model', 'Oracle Fusion Cloud Procurement offers a direct cXML supplier PunchOut source as well as Oracle-native XML models. Confirm the buyer uses the cXML path supported by PunchOut Central.'],
  ['Identify the buying unit', 'The Oracle catalog administrator sets up a PunchOut catalog for a procurement business unit. Confirm which buyer entity and supplier catalog should be linked.'],
  ['Return requisition lines', 'The requester shops the supplier site and returns items to Oracle Self Service Procurement as requisition lines.'],
  ['Receive an approved PO', 'After the buyer’s requisition process, confirm how the approved PO reaches PunchOut Central before a Shopify order is created.']
];
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview"><div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
    <div class="page-hero__copy reveal"><span class="ey">Shopify Oracle Procurement PunchOut</span><h1>Connect Oracle procurement to a Shopify supplier catalog.</h1><p class="lead">Oracle Fusion Cloud Procurement can open a supplier-hosted PunchOut catalog and return selected items to a requisition. PunchOut Central supports the direct cXML connection path to your existing Shopify store.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss an Oracle connection &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#details">Review the catalog model &darr;</a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-visual logo-hero reveal"><div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Buyer system</span><b>Direct cXML model</b></div><div class="logo-hero__mark"><img src="/assets/logos/oracle.svg" alt="Oracle"></div><span class="logo-hero__status">PunchOut Central</span><h3>Oracle to Shopify</h3><p>Requester catalog access and requisition on the buyer side.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="flow"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">Oracle workflow</span><h2>Return the cart to the Purchase Requisitions work area.</h2><p class="lead">Oracle describes a requester opening a supplier site from a PunchOut link, choosing products, then returning items to the requisition for editing and submission.</p></div>
    <div class="integration-flow reveal"><div class="integration-node"><strong>Oracle Procurement</strong><span>Requisition and approval</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node integration-node--accent"><strong>PunchOut Central</strong><span>cXML buyer connection</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node"><strong>Shopify</strong><span>Supplier-hosted catalog</span></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="details"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Buyer onboarding</span><h2>Confirm Oracle’s direct cXML supplier source.</h2><p class="lead">Oracle supports more than one PunchOut model. PunchOut Central’s documented protocols are cXML and OCI; this page describes the Oracle direct cXML path, not Oracle-native XML support.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid">{plan.map(([title, description], index) => <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="proof"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Validation</span><h2>Test the exact catalog and buying unit.</h2><p class="lead">Ask the buyer to verify the PunchOut link, cXML launch, returned requisition lines, approval and PO delivery. Match the approved PO to the Shopify order and invoice record; do not treat the returned cart as an order.</p></div>
    <div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/cxml/"><span>Protocol</span><h3>cXML PunchOut</h3><p>Review the supported procurement protocol.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/shopify/"><span>Supplier side</span><h3>Shopify integration</h3><p>See how the store supplies the catalog.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/how-it-works/"><span>Transaction</span><h3>How it works</h3><p>Follow approval, PO, order and invoice.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a></div>
    <p><small>Buyer-side references: <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/cloud/saas/procurement/26d/oapro/punchout-catalogs.html">Oracle Punchout Catalogs</a> and <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/cloud/saas/procurement/26d/oapro/create-a-punchout-catalog-with-a-direct-cxml-supplier-punchout-source.html">direct cXML supplier source</a>.</small></p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="faq"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>Oracle Procurement questions</h2></div><div class="faq reveal">
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does PunchOut Central support Oracle-native XML?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>This page covers Oracle’s direct cXML supplier PunchOut model. Oracle-native XML support is not claimed.</p></div></div>
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>What returns to Oracle after shopping?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>The selected items return as requisition lines for the buyer’s review and submission, not as a Shopify order.</p></div></div>
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>What about invoices?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>PunchOut Central tracks invoice activity with the transaction. Confirm the buyer’s invoice-delivery requirements separately.</p></div></div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">Confirm the Oracle model</span><h2>Review the buyer’s cXML catalog setup with us.</h2><p class="lead">Share the procurement business unit, PunchOut source and Shopify store involved.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/integrations/procurement-systems/">Explore buyer systems</a></div></div></section>
</main>
